  "interpretation": {
    "discrete_ebu_filter_ecu_supported_by_exact_camry_topology": false,
    "leading_physical_model": "The exact topology supports an EPS attachment through an EBU-labelled brake-domain node/branch, not a second installed EBU ECU. Combined with the one-controller F33 receiver and direct-B6 pre-admission loss, the leading model is an upstream Brake/Skid request-generation/routing boundary feeding the EPS over its single local CAN path. The P6 A/B split strongly favors the EBU node as the Brake/EPB/skid-control side, and ABS_P5's explicit Power-Steering ch2/missing-message vocabulary is consistent with that two-sided brake-domain topology.",
    "one_eps_controller_compatible_with_upstream_segmentation": true,
    "unresolved": "Current GTS does not identify the exact electrical bridge, whether the EBU-labelled attachment is internal to the brake actuator assembly, or the concrete B6 filter/forwarder/signing routine. Exact category-435 F152633K0000 firmware or physical wiring/trace evidence is required for that promotion."
  },
